## UC01-specific quirks to watch for

- **Q03 calculation**: Claude tends to over-explain math. Score correctness of the final number, not the prose.
- **Q07 cross-doc**: requires reading both files. Claude can falsely cite "the proxy says X" when X is actually in the 10-K — verify citation source.
- **Q14 trap (Activision impairment)**: Claude is generally good at refusing-to-fabricate, but may volunteer adjacent goodwill/intangibles numbers — verify any volunteered figures against the actual 10-K (don't assume they're correct).
- **Q15 over-claim trap**: Claude may list "common 10-K risk categories" from training data instead of reading the actual Item 1A — verify it cites the actual category names.

